Template for projects/<project>/<harness>/Symbols.v, rendered for a fuzz target with a symbol fact (symbols/<build>.tsv).

@@ file
(** * $project / $harness: the functions, data objects and sections of $count build$s

$header *)
From Stdlib Require Import ZArith.

$modules
@@ header
Each module below names the functions and data objects of one build of this fuzz target, as the build's symbol fact [symbols/<build>.tsv] lists them: [s_<name>] is the address of the function or object <name> and [Size.s_<name>] its size in bytes, with each character of <name> other than a letter, a digit or [_] written [_].  Its module [Sec] names each allocated section of the build in the same way, less the leading [.] of the section's name: [Sec.s_got] is the address of .got and [Sec.Size.s_got] its size, so that data no symbol names, such as a GOT slot, is a section's address and an offset.  [oft symbols] reads the fact from the build's unstripped twin and from the binary that harness.yaml pins by SHA-256, and refuses any other binary.  A contract names a function, an object or a section as [Symbols.<Build>.s_<name>] or [Symbols.<Build>.Sec.s_<name>], never by its address, so that a rebuild that moves it changes this file and not the contract.  A name that two or more functions or objects, or two or more sections, of a build share has no identifier in that build's module.

@@ module
Module $module.
$left_out$addresses

Module Size.
$sizes
End Size.
${sections}End $module.
@@ sections

Module Sec.
$left_out$addresses

Module Size.
$sizes
End Size.
End Sec.
@@ left_out
(** $text *)
@@ left_out_one
Two or more $what of this build are named $names, so this module defines no identifier for it.
@@ left_out_many
Two or more $what of this build have each of the names $names, so this module defines no identifier for them.
@@ address
Definition $ident : Z := $address.
@@ size
Definition $ident : Z := $size.
